{
  "version": 1,
  "notes": [
    "keyId = base64url(SHA-256 of the 65 decoded bytes of the uncompressed P-256 point). Never hash the base64url string: notKeyId lists that wrong value per point and every implementation must refuse to match it.",
    "Signed mint message: UTF-8 of tag, origin, keyId, nonce and decimal expiresAt joined by LF, no trailing newline. The nonce is signed as its base64url string, never decoded. origin is scheme://host[:port] with no trailing slash.",
    "Signature: ECDSA P-256 over SHA-256 of that message, ASN.1 DER, then base64url. High-S is accepted and raw r||s is refused, exactly as in approval-proof.json; Swift and Java must send whatever the platform signs and never normalise S.",
    "Result bodies: ok true carries an optional result and no error or code; ok false carries a code, an optional short error and no result. The JSON of the result is at most 262144 bytes (job.oversize); larger is refused with 413 and the phone may send code too_large instead.",
    "Registration: the device id comes from the bearer, never the body. A phone sends only the keys shown; any other key, protocol other than 1 or capability value outside the catalog is refused with 400."
  ],
